{"name":"Cellar Door","hex":"#75553f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cellar door","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A door leading to a cellar.","The part of a winery from which wine may be sampled or purchased."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cellar_door"}],"entries":[{"title":"Phonaesthetics","blocks":[{"text":"Phonaesthetics is the study of the beauty and pleasantness associated with the sounds of certain words or parts of words. The term was first used in this sense, perhaps by J. R. R. Tolkien, during the mid-20th century and derives from Ancient Greek  φωνή (phōnḗ) 'voice, sound' and  αἰσθητική (aisthētikḗ) 'aesthetics'. Speech sounds have many aesthetic qualities, some of which are subjectively regarded as euphonious (pleasing) or cacophonous (displeasing). Phonaesthetics remains a budding and often subjective field of study, with no scientifically or otherwise formally established definition; today, it mostly exists as a marginal branch of psychology, phonetics, or poetics."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phonaesthetics"},{"title":"Glossary of wine terms","blocks":[{"text":"The glossary of wine terms lists the definitions of many general terms used within the wine industry. For terms specific to viticulture, winemaking, grape varieties, and wine tasting, see the topic specific list in the \"See also\" section below."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glossary_of_wine_terms"},{"title":"Cellar Door (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cellar Door is a 2024 American thriller film written by Sam Scott and Lori Evans Taylor, directed by Vaughn Stein and starring Jordana Brewster, Scott Speedman, Laurence Fishburne and Addison Timlin."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/67/Cellar_Door_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cellar_Door_(film)"},{"title":"Door","blocks":[{"text":"A door is a hinged or otherwise movable barrier that allows ingress (entry) into and egress (exit) from an enclosure. The created opening in the wall is a doorway or portal. A door's essential and primary purpose is to provide security by controlling access to the doorway (portal). Conventionally, it is a panel that fits into the doorway of a building, room, or vehicle. Doors are generally made of a material suited to the door's task. They are commonly attached by hinges, but can move by other means, such as slides or counterbalancing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/L-door.png/330px-L-door.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Door"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Hobbit_hole_with_red_door.jpg/500px-Hobbit_hole_with_red_door.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Hobbit_hole_with_red_door.jpg/1280px-Hobbit_hole_with_red_door.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Hobbit_hole_with_red_door.jpg/500px-Hobbit_hole_with_red_door.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The entrance of the \"hobbit hole\", which Tolkien devised, is a type of \"cellar door\", the idea of whose phonetic beauty he popularized.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHobbit_hole_with_red_door.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Lightmatter_wine_barrels.jpg/500px-Lightmatter_wine_barrels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Lightmatter_wine_barrels.jpg/500px-Lightmatter_wine_barrels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wine barre